// Cross 1/7 of the height, the fields at the pole square, the outer fields 7/4 of their
// length. On a height of 28: cross 4, square fields 12, outer fields 21, so 12:4:21 by
// 12:4:12 and a length of 37.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Denmark"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  source "https://www.retsinformation.dk/api/pdf/246718"
  source "https://www.folketingstidende.dk/samling/20241/lovforslag/L21/20241_L21_som_fremsat.pdf"
  source "https://www.crwflags.com/fotw/flags/dk.html"
  source "https://snl.no/Danmarks_flagg_og_v%C3%A5pen"
  source "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag_of_Denmark"
  note "The 2024 law says only that the national flag is Dannebrog. It gives no geometry."
  note "The geometry is in the government's remarks on bill L 21 of 2024, under section 1, which aren't law. They give the cross as 1/7 of the height at the staff, square fields there, and outer fields 1 3/4 times the inner ones. FOTW and Store norske leksikon report the same 28:37."
  note "FOTW reports the older figures too: a regulation of 1748 has outer fields of 6/4, or 14:17, and a statement of 1893 tolerated up to 7/4 without canceling it. The Defence Ministry's ceremonial book is reported with 14:17. None of these was read, and FOTW and Wikipedia date the 1748 regulation differently, to 11 July and 11 June."
  note "Pantone 186 C is in the same remarks, and FOTW and Wikipedia report it from DS 359:2005, which wasn't read. The hex and CMYK values are the Album des Pavillons 2023's for that Pantone, as reported by FOTW. White is plain white."
  note "This is the rectangular stutflag, not the state's swallow-tailed splitflag."
  law "Act No. 1449 of 10 December 2024 on flying flags, section 1" {
    source "https://www.retsinformation.dk/api/pdf/246718"
  }
}
palette {
  red "#c8102e" {
    pantone "186 C"
    cmyk 14 100 79 4
  }
  white "#ffffff"
}
proportion hoist=28 fly=37

field red
cross white {
  fly 12 4 21
  hoist 12 4 12
}
